e home section.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summary\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mLocating\u001b[12Gseed\u001b[17Gscript\u001b[24Gsections\u001b[33Gto\u001b[36Gchange\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ cd /home/lina-wolf/projects/typo3/t3ca-2026/demo && grep -n \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\"existing(\\|process(\\[\\|NEWhomeEvents\\|'additional'\\|templateLayout\\|^echo\\|^\\]);\" \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1BBuild/I\u001b[14Gitialisation/seed-events.php; cat \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mpackages/mtosafi_sitepackage/Re\u001b[38Gources/Private/Extensions/News/Partials/List/Pagination.html | head \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B-5\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87m✶\u001b[3GMetamorphosing… \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(30s · ↓\u001b[28G2.7k tokens)\r\u001b[1B  ⎿  Tip: Use /btw to ask a side qu\u001b[37Gstion without interrupting Claude\u001b[39m\u001b[31;1H\u001b[29;3H\u001b[?25h"]
[1296.541246, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G \u001b[5Gbefore eventnews was installed, so it allows none\u001b[55Gof the new fields: \u001b[75Ge\u001b[77Gthe\u001b[81G \"Is event\" nor the\u001b[K\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bregistr\u001b[13Gtion\u001b[18Gfields. On a fresh install the group \u001b[56Gs created after the fields\u001b[83Gexist and get\u001b[97G them\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bautomatically. He\u001b[23Ge, someone has\u001b[38Gto\u001b[41Gtick\u001b[46Gthem\u001b[51Gin\u001b[54Gthe\u001b[58Ggroup\u001b[64G(System\u001b[72G>\u001b[74GBackend\u001b[82Gusers),\u001b[90Gor\u001b[93GI\u001b[95Gcan\u001b[99Gadd\u001b[103Gthem\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B \u001b[5Gfor you.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mThe fresh-install proof still hasn't run.\u001b[22m The n\u001b[53Gw \u001b[38;2;177;185;249mdata.xml\u001b[64G\u001b[39mhasn't\u001b[71Gbeen\u001b[76Gimported\u001b[85Ganywhere\u001b[94Gyet.\u001b[99GIt\u001b[102Gneeds\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bthe\u001b[9Gdatabase\u001b[18Gemptied,\u001b[27Gwhich\u001b[33Gauto\u001b[38Gmode\u001b[43Gblocked\u001b[51Gearlier,\u001b[60Gso\u001b[63Git's\u001b[68Gyour\u001b[73Gcall.\u001b[79GThe\u001b[83Gfull\u001b[88Gfresh-install\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  steps\u001b[11Gare in the root README.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mI haven't opened the event form in the backend.\u001b[53G\u001b[22mI\u001b[55Gchecked\u001b[63Gthe\u001b[67Gdatabase\u001b[76Gcolumns,\u001b[85Gthe\u001b[89Gexport\u001b[96Gand\u001b[100Gthe\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G  frontend, but not how the fields look\u001b[43Gin\u001b[46Gthe\u001b[50Gevent\u001b[56Gform.\r\u001b[2B  Nothing is committed. Should I show you the diff and a commit message?\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GCogitated for 2\u001b[19G 54s · done 7:32 PM\r\u001b[2B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mthe events are on the news page and when you use de breadcrumb you only see news not events\u001b[39m             \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[39m I'm giving events their own pages that mirror the news setup, with\u001b[70Ga\u001b[72Gbreadcrumb\u001b[83Gof\u001b[86GHome\u001b[91G›\u001b[93GEvents\u001b[100G›\u001b[102GEvent\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Band an \"All events\" link on the home section.\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · summary\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mReading Build/Initialisation/seed-events.php\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Build/Initialisation/seed-events.php\u001b[39m\u001b[31;1H\u001b[29;3H\u001b[?25h"]
